  "conclusions": [
    "Repeated Chamfer-only C1/C2 runs diverge at the first prior output despite byte-exact initial tensors and prior input/style. This precedes every semantic probe and proves exact whole-trajectory parity is not attainable under the observed native execution policy.",
    "Chamfer-only numerical drift amplifies through the actual first local/style gradients, later trajectories, decoded geometry and predictions; it is not merely a hash formatting difference.",
    "C1/KL0 also diverges before semantic activation. Three unaligned full trajectories cannot isolate an additional zero-weight semantic contribution or justify an arbitrary numerical tolerance.",
    "No source, GPU state, parity gate or coefficient was changed by this CPU audit."
  ],
